---
title: Chi Chi's Corn Cake
cookTime: 10 mins
totalTime: 10 mins
Rating: 10/10
source: http://allrecipes.com/recipe/chi-chis-corn-cake/
tags: Sides, Copycat
---

Preheat oven to 350°F.

In a medium bowl, beat @butter{1/2%cup} with an electric mixer until creamy.
Add @masa harina{1/3%cup}(corn flour) and @water{1/4%cup} and beat until well combined.

In food processor or blender, process @whole kernel corn{1 1/2%cups} in short pulses to coarsely chop.
Leave several pieces of whole corn.
Stir the processed corn and the @cornmeal{1/4%cup} into the butter mixture.

In a separate bowl, stir together @sugar{1/3%cup}, @heavy cream{2%tbsp}, @salt{1/4%tsp},
and @baking powder{1/2%tsp} until well combined.
Stir sugar mixture into butter mixture and pour all into a #9x9-inch baking dish{}.
Cover with foil.

Place baking dish in a #roasting pan{}, and place roasting pan on oven rack.
Fill roasting pan with @water{2%cups}(boiling) to reach halfway up the sides of the baking dish.

Bake ~{50-60%minutes}, or until pick inserted in center comes out clean.
Remove baking dish from water bath and let rest ~{10%minutes}.

Serve using ice cream scoop or large spoon.
